      "math_academy_id": "q-130043",
      "sequence_position": 19,
      "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$, where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{y},\\, & \\text{if}\\,-1<x<2,\\,1<y<e, \\\\ xy,\\, & \\text{if}\\,2<x<4,\\,1<y<e,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that we have $R={R}_{1}\\cup {R}_{2}$, where ${R}_{1}=(-1,2)\\times (1,e)$ and ${R}_{2}=(2,4)\\times (1,e).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A= & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}(3{x}^{2})(\\frac{1}{y})\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}(x)(y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{-1}^{2}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y)+({\\int }_{2}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{e}y\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}]_{-1}^{2}\\cdot [\\operatorname{ln}⁡y]_{1}^{e}+{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{2}^{4}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =(8+1)\\cdot (1-0)+(8-2)\\cdot (\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =9+3({e}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =3{e}^{2}+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
